## Story Description
Implement src/models/database.py defining all SQLite tables using SQLAlchemy Core (not ORM) and providing helper functions for database operations. Schema must be Postgres-compatible — no SQLite-specific types.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: src/models/database.py — define metadata = MetaData() and SQLAlchemy Table objects for: transactions_table (all canonical CanonicalTransaction fields as columns; raw_data as TEXT; use TEXT for strings, FLOAT for floats, INTEGER for ints, TEXT for dates stored as ISO strings), supplier_master_table (canonical_supplier_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, canonical_name TEXT, parent_company_id TEXT, parent_name TEXT, country TEXT, identifiers TEXT, created_at TEXT, updated_at TEXT), supplier_match_log_table (id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, raw_supplier_name TEXT, raw_supplier_id TEXT, canonical_supplier_id TEXT, match_method TEXT, confidence FLOAT, evidence TEXT, review_status TEXT, created_at TEXT), category_overrides_table (id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, canonical_supplier_id TEXT, gl_account TEXT, override_l1 TEXT, override_l2 TEXT, override_l3 TEXT, unspsc_code TEXT, reviewer TEXT, reason TEXT, created_at TEXT), audit_log_table (id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, table_name TEXT, record_id TEXT, field_name TEXT, old_value TEXT, new_value TEXT, changed_by TEXT, changed_at TEXT)
- Implement get_engine(db_path: str) -> Engine using create_engine(f'sqlite:///{db_path}', connect_args={'check_same_thread': False})
- Implement init_db(engine: Engine) -> None that calls metadata.create_all(engine)
