## Story Description
Create all reference data CSV and YAML files in data/reference/. These are bundled with the application. The UNSPSC file should be a representative ~500-commodity subset. FX rates cover 2023-2025 monthly averages for 8 currencies. Seed mappings include ~200 supplier/GL/keyword-to-category mappings.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Create data/reference/unspsc_v24.csv with columns: segment_code, segment_name, family_code, family_name, class_code, class_name, commodity_code, commodity_name. Minimum 400 rows. Cover segments: 44 (Office/Photo/Film), 43 (IT/Broadcasting), 78 (Transportation/Storage), 80 (Management/Business), 81 (Engineering/R&D), 72 (Building/Construction), 76 (Industrial Cleaning), 51 (Drugs/Pharma/Biotech), 50 (Food/Beverage/Tobacco), 53 (Apparel/Luggage/Personal), 73 (Industrial Production/Manufacturing), 55 (Published Products). Use realistic 8-digit commodity codes following the UNSPSC pattern (segment 2 digits + family 2 + class 2 + commodity 2).
- Create data/reference/fx_rates.csv with columns: year_month, from_ccy, to_ccy, rate. Cover 2023-01 through 2025-12 for all bidirectional pairs: AUD↔USD, AUD↔EUR, AUD↔GBP, AUD↔SGD, AUD↔NZD, AUD↔JPY, AUD↔CNY. Use realistic rates: AUD/USD ~0.63-0.68, AUD/EUR ~0.58-0.62, AUD/GBP ~0.50-0.54, AUD/SGD ~0.85-0.92, AUD/NZD ~1.07-1.12, AUD/JPY ~90-100, AUD/CNY ~4.5-4.8. Minimum 36 months × 14 pairs = 504 rows.
- Create data/reference/legal_suffixes.yaml as a YAML list under key 'suffixes'. Include at minimum 40 entries covering: 'Pty Ltd', 'Pty. Ltd.', 'Pty. Ltd', 'P/L', 'P.L.', 'LLC', 'L.L.C.', 'Inc', 'Inc.', 'Incorporated', 'Ltd', 'Ltd.', 'Limited', 'GmbH', 'AG', 'S.A.', 'S.A.S.', 'B.V.', 'N.V.', 'PLC', 'Plc', 'Corp', 'Corp.', 'Corporation', 'Co', 'Co.', 'Company', 'Trust', 'Pty', 'Holdings', 'Group', 'International', 'Trading', 'Services', 'Solutions', 'Aust', 'Australia', 'Global' (as standalone suffix tokens)
